WEBVTT

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.320
We'll see each other again, right?

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.240
Yeah.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.590
After-School Pleiades

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.760
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:44.230
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:50.610
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:56.160
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.410
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:08.460
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.260
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.340
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.430
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.140
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.020
We'll open the promised door

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.190
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.140
Has she joined the gardening club?

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.430
Why, all of a sudden?

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.980
Subaru's primary field is astronomy, isn't it?

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.230
And look at the way she works.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.400
She's clumsy.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.990
But she's treating them with lots of care.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.030
Aoi, have you heard anything?

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.120
No, not really.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.410
Really? That's surprising...

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.250
It is?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.130
I thought you'd know everything about Subaru.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.000
Of course I don't.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.970
Subaru looks like she's changed.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.100
Changed? How so? In what way?

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.230
It's hard to say specifically...

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.770
But I've never seen her look so troubled.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.520
That's true.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:02.530
Two Treasures or The Smell of Strawberries

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.640
Subaru!

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.890
Aoi?

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.150
Here.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:36.400
Drink this and cheer up.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.150
Did I look like I was down?

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:42.570
Well...

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.070
Yeah.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.750
Other way, Subaru.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.710
When you aren't panicking like that,
it throws us off.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.590
What do you mean?

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:02.090
Knowing you, you lost something again, right?

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.850
I'll help you look for it,
so don't bear it all yourself.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.180
Thanks.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:16.310
Um, I lost a place, or a person...
Well, it's both, actually...

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:29.830
It was never a specific spot.
They were always different.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.790
And I only knew the person's name...

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.630
Hold on, you aren't talking about a dream, right?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.670
This place actually existed?

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.420
Yeah, I think it did...

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.640
You think? You don't know?

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:52.520
I'm not really sure anymore that it even happened.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.520
Huh?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.480
Huh? Sorry... That's strange...

00:04:59.150 --> 00:04:59.980
Subaru...

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.530
Why didn't you say anything?

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.240
Huh?

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.160
You could've told me.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.540
Aoi!

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.210
You forgot your wallet.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.800
<i>I wanted to change!</i>

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.470
<i>That's why I'm here, and yet...</i>

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.360
<i>I'm just doing the same things over again.</i>

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.570
<i>Why am I so...</i>

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.790
Subaru?

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.500
What's wrong?

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.750
I lost the keychain I made with my mom.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:06.840
I put it on my bag this morning, but when
I looked just now, it wasn't there...

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.260
Don't cry, Subaru.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.510
You'll be in middle school next year, you know.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.760
Come on, I'll help you look for it.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:17.810
Okay.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.530
Why? I watered them...

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.530
Could you move?

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.410
Huh?

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.880
I'm sorry!

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.460
Are you all ri—

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:49.470
The water...

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:01.600
To plant these flowers in dirt,
you need to make them grow new roots.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.030
You cut the stalk in water,
and after replanting it,

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.820
you give it occasional sunlight...

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.030
Are you listening?

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.700
Oh, yes! But, um...

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.280
What?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.120
Minato, what's with your outfit?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:16.910
What about it?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:20.000
You don't look like you usually do.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.050
Oh, sorry!

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:29.420
It's my first time seeing you
anywhere other than that place...

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.180
I was just a little surprised.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.430
That place?

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.930
The greenhouse.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.430
This school doesn't have a greenhouse.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.440
Hey, new kid!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.900
We're changing classrooms for the afternoon.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:46.690
Minato...

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:48.860
What's with that outfit?

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.700
When did you join the gardening club?

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:54.740
Subarun! What are you doing?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.950
We're meeting in the club room!

00:07:58.580 --> 00:07:59.790
Sorry I'm late—

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:01.460
Whoa, it's so bright!

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.130
Subaru, are you all right?

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:05.840
What is all this? Why?

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:09.210
Hey, president, shift the angle of the window.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:16.430
Space is outside the window! Why?!

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:21.100
With the fragments we've collected,
my power has grown progressively stronger.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.430
Amazing, isn't it?

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.230
Sometimes this macaron is useful.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.850
Now we can access space more directly.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.400
Then was that bright thing earlier the Sun?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.270
That was Mercury!

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.440
This window is currently located
between the Sun and Mercury.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.660
It shines brightly by reflecting the Sun's light.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.080
Wow, so Mercury was shining?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.580
Oh, the light's back!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.700
Another... Mercury?

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:45.540
No, no... Not Mercury, just a comet.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.790
Subaru, transform.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:07.060
Oh, I forgot to mention this,

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:11.110
but if you go out into space too abruptly,
your ears will ring, so be careful.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.400
Magic really is convenient...

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.110
Uh, so what about today's fragment?

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.530
All right, now!

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.460
We're going to ride it!

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.840
It feels like the comet is pushing us.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.470
This is a real comet.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:38.970
The Sun...

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.220
Amazing.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.100
Given our distance from the Sun,
the speed of the comet...

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.850
This is unexpectedly...

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.140
So, president, what do we do now?

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:50.520
Oh... Actually, the fragment
we must capture today

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.480
is the object we're riding right now.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:53.820
Wait, you mean...

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:56.780
This comet's the fragment?

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:14.380
I can only speculate as to how the fragment
became a part of this comet, but...

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:19.390
Well, I think it probably froze when it
shot through a gas giant or something.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:24.010
So the fragment became coated in ice,
and then became a comet.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.390
It's kind of like a chocolate truffle.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.350
It looks more like cotton candy, though.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:32.150
Then we need to get the fragment
out from inside this somehow?

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.860
That would be the case.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.240
Now, we can't afford to take our time.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.070
If we don't hurry...

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.110
The fragment...

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.410
Huh?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:41.740
You're right!

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.660
The fragment is emerging on its own?

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:48.410
I think the comet's core might be
melting from the Sun's heat?

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:51.170
I see... Since it's ice, it's weak to heat.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:55.210
Then if we wait, the fragment
will come out on its own.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.170
No, I don't think that will work.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.380
Why not?

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.590
Because it's on course to shoot into the Sun.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:05.220
You mean... it'll fall into the Sun
along with the fragment?

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:09.600
If it does, are you saying we'll have
to go into that fire to get it?

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:14.520
That's why I'm trying to think of a way
to stop the comet from falling.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.860
What if we pull the fragment from
behind so it won't fall into the Sun?

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.990
Um, we might want to do the reverse.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:22.700
If we don't increase the speed,

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:25.580
won't the Sun's gravity just draw it in?

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.750
Are we pushing or pulling?

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.660
I think we're already falling.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.000
What?!

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.880
Hey, look at that.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:37.380
Something seems strange about the Sun...

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:40.970
An explosion?

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.130
It's a solar prominence!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:45.220
We don't want to take a direct hit!
That's a bit too hot!

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:49.730
No other choice! Break away!

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.830
I'll take that fragment.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.740
Ugh, trouble!

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.120
Whoa, wai—

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.420
Aoi!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:20.760
Are you all right?

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.220
Aoi?

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.220
Sorry.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.730
It's fine, as long as you're okay.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.560
Not that. I'm sorry.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.560
Huh?

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.610
I know it, too.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.440
I can't stay like this.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.070
I want to change, but...

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.070
Me, too!

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.450
You little...

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.670
Where are Subaru and Aoi?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:58.960
There.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:01.710
What are they doing, at a time like this?

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.930
Don't they both seem a little different than usual?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:05.970
Different how?

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.930
They hadn't said a word to each other
since we met in the club room.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.600
Are their stars in retrograde?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:17.600
<i>That winter, the first snow had fallen,</i>

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.900
<i>and Aoi and I were walking
on our usual road home.</i>

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.650
<i>Aoi didn't tell me that, come spring,</i>

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.990
<i>she'd be going to a different school.</i>

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:37.880
<i>I thought maybe I'd been holding
her back the whole time.</i>

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.340
<i>But...</i>

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.500
<i>I was too afraid to ask.</i>

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.850
<i>I could only watch as the footprints that had</i>

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:55.180
<i>walked alongside mine stretched on,
one by one, farther and farther away.</i>

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:59.610
<i>I'm sure that was the moment our footprints</i>

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:01.860
<i>went their separate ways.</i>

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:08.950
Aoi, why didn't you say anything?

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:12.830
How am I supposed to know that?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:13.830
What about you?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.080
You left me behind without saying anything!

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.880
<i>I always thought I was helping Subaru,</i>

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:27.840
<i>but countless times, I wondered if I was
just doing it to satisfy my own ego.</i>

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.430
We're both the ones who were left behind.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:39.850
That's why neither of us has the answer, right?

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:47.570
We both just wanted to be together, and yet...

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:52.070
We were finally able to meet here, and yet...

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.080
Subaru...

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:58.790
Stupid Subaru! Stupid Aoi!

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.540
After coming this far,
what is there to hesitate about?

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.630
The two of you should understand.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.800
By drawing together, your fortune rises.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:08.260
Everyone...

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:10.800
We have to go.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:12.800
Let's go, Aoi!

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:14.930
Yeah!

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:21.520
Jeez, you're so persistent!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:28.740
No, I won't let you leave.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:30.280
Don't interfere!

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:39.450
It's like it's dancing on top of the fire.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.290
What do you think we should do?

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:47.500
I won't let you get any closer to my fragment!

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.510
Subaru!

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.350
Subaru...

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.900
Subaru, you can fly, right?

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:09.570
Yeah!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:14.740
What?

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.160
You haven't finished with me yet!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:19.830
I won't let you get in their way.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.960
Head to those two...

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:32.970
I'm counting on you for the fragment...

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.300
Roger!

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.350
I found it!

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.310
I found it, Subaru!

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:49.820
See? It's this, right?

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:52.690
Here.

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.110
Don't lose it again.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:57.780
Here.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.410
I was going to give this to you, Aoi.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:10.800
<i>No matter when or where,
or how much Subaru may change,</i>

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.970
<i>the important thing that will never change</i>

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:14.720
<i> is right here.</i>

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:25.980
<i>Aoi will always help me when I need it.</i>

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:31.020
<i>That's why I have to change, so one day,
I can protect Aoi, too.</i>

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:32.900
I found it!

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.990
I found it, Subaru!

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.870
Aoi, thank you!

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.620
If you lose it again, I'll help you find it again.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:45.500
I won't lose it again!

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.330
I'll find it as many times as you need.

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:49.500
I'll never, ever lose it again!

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.050
I'm going to treasure it!

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.270
<i>Both of us</i>

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:07.190
<i>can change.</i>

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.980
One, two...

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:26.790
This fragment looks like the Ursa Minor
keychain I helped you find a long time ago.

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.170
It does.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:32.090
Both this fragment and that keychain
are things I was able to retrieve

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.550
because you were there for me.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.510
I can't have you rescuing me all the time, after all.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.050
Same here.

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:43.470
Oh, but I'll always like being with you!

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:45.020
Subaru...

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.730
I know.

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:54.110
No matter where we go or how much we change,
you'll still be you, and I'll still be me.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:56.400
Aoi...

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.990
Yeah, that's right.

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.450
All's well that ends well, huh?

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.960
Jeez, I worried about them for nothing.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.960
That isn't true. They have both changed.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.000
Yes. In a very good way.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.550
Hmm... Well, maybe.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:25.720
Immature souls like yours

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:29.100
have no right to touch those.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:34.980
See you tomorrow!

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:34.980
Bye!

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.610
Later!

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.610
See you tomorrow!

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:40.740
Oh, right!

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:42.990
Here.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.120
Huh?

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.120
This is...

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:50.210
There was another one?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.250
No, there was only one.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.630
They're the same thing.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:58.380
See? This missing part here is exactly the same.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:00.720
I wonder why that is...

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.430
Oh!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.050
I see.

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:05.640
Yeah.

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:09.720
Neither of us was left behind.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:15.860
That's right. We both received a
treasure from a precious friend.

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.090
Minato!

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.430
What is it? Why are you shouting?

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.430
I still think that outfit looks a little strange!

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:53.100
Wha—

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.610
You're rude, you know.

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:57.770
Also, here!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:02.530
You like this, right?

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:09.740
Don't you ever think you're mistaking me for
someone, or misunderstanding something?

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:14.210
I might have changed into
someone you don't know.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:17.290
I could practically be a different person.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:19.880
Yeah, that may be.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:23.340
But my friend taught me something.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:24.300
So...

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.930
You'll always be Minato.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.060
And once again, just like always,

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:35.770
you manage to find the key to the door somehow...

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:43.440
We meet again, Minato.

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.950
To Be Continued

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:01.590
You see, when I looked up

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:06.970
everyone was smiling at me

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:16.690
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:25.650
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:23.020
...my daily life...

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:35.410
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:37.290
"Can I fly?"

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:41.500
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:47.130
We can go there whenever we want to

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:56.810
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:22:56.810 --> 00:23:01.440
"We have to catch them!"

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:05.940
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:11.280
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:15.990
sometime after school

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.460
Y-Yeah...

00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:26.460
Huh?

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:29.670
Ah, I don't understand what you're saying!

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:31.840
Next episode: Nanako 13.

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.350
Nanako, come back!
